    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-012",
      "title": "Causative and perception verbs with an infinitive",
      "explanation": "Mandar, deixar, fazer and the perception verbs ver, ouvir and sentir take an object and then an infinitive: ela me fez rir, eu os ouvi cantar, ele nos deixou sair. The object comes before the infinitive and is the infinitive's subject. In standard written Portuguese the object is a clitic (me, nos, o, a, os, as) and the infinitive stays uninflected. Do not turn the infinitive into a conjugated form or a gerund after the causative: ela me fez rir, not ela me fez rindo. Written style may place the clitic after the main verb (deixou-nos sair).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "pt": "Ela me fez rir.",
          "en": "She made me laugh."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Eu os ouvi cantar.",
          "en": "I heard them sing."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Ele nos deixou sair.",
          "en": "He let us leave."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["COE-CV20"],
