    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-014",
      "title": "Participial clauses",
      "explanation": "A participial clause puts the past participle first and the noun after it, and it states that something is finished before the main action: terminado o trabalho, saímos. The participle agrees in gender and number with the noun that follows: terminada a reunião, terminados os exames, feitas as contas. Dito isso and feito isso are fixed forms. This is formal, written style. Do not leave the participle invariable (terminado a reunião is wrong) and do not swap in the gerund when the point is completion: terminando o trabalho describes simultaneous action.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "pt": "Terminado o trabalho, saímos.",
          "en": "Once the work was finished, we left."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Terminada a reunião, todos saíram.",
          "en": "Once the meeting was over, everyone left."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Dito isso, ele saiu.",
          "en": "That said, he left."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["COE-CV20"],
      "version": {
