      "title": "Infinitive or subjunctive after verbs of will and hope",
      "explanation": "After verbs of wanting, hoping, preferring and asking, Portuguese chooses by subject. When the subject is the same, use the infinitive: quero sair, ela espera ganhar, nós precisamos estudar. When the subjects differ, use que plus the subjunctive: quero que você saia, ele prefere que nós fiquemos, ela pediu que eles esperassem. Do not use que with an infinitive (quero que sair is wrong), and do not use a bare subject plus infinitive in standard writing after querer (quero você sair is wrong). After a past main verb the subjunctive is imperfect.",
